"""Country calling codes and how long a national number can be after each.

A number written with a leading ``+`` starts with one of about two hundred
calling codes, no one of which is the beginning of another, and each country
allows only certain lengths after it. That is enough to tell ``+33 1 23 45
67 89`` from ``+10 2026 10 08`` without knowing how any country groups its
digits.
"""

